by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-14T12:40:09Z

Moving the review notes out of the description, for the record. What changed in the July rework:

* **the accessors take real parameters.** `getSerializedName()` and friends were reading an undeclared argument through `func_get_arg()`, which is what made PHPStan red with 16 errors and made `getSerializedName('a')` emit a raw `foreach()` warning. `AttributeMetadata` is `@final`, so the class now declares `array $groups = ['*']` with `@param list<string>` and only the interface keeps the commented-out form, as @xabbuh asked.
* **an empty `groups` array is refused.** `new SerializedName('x', [])` silently meant "every group", giving two ways to say the same thing, which @xabbuh asked to reject. It now throws and points at omitting the argument. Absent groups in YAML or XML still mean every group, which is a default rather than a second spelling.
* **the YAML loader no longer drops falsy names.** `if ($serializedName = $line[...] ?? false)` skipped `'0'` and `''` entirely, so `'0'` was lost and the `MappingException` below it was unreachable. It now uses `isset()`, so `'0'` round trips and `''` is rejected. The same fix later went into the per-group list for paths.
* **YAML validates the mapping shape.** `groups: a` instead of a list produced a raw `foreach()` warning and silently dropped the mapping; `groups: ['']` and `groups: [1]` created groups named `''` and `'1'`. All three now raise a `MappingException` naming the file, the attribute and the class.
* **a warm metadata cache survives the upgrade.** `__serialize()` renamed two keys with no `__unserialize()`, so a payload written by 8.1 produced `Creation of dynamic property` deprecations and then `getSerializedName()` returned `null` where it used to return the configured name. A shim now maps the old single-value keys onto the per-group arrays.
* **the normalizer half is tested.** Reverting only `AbstractObjectNormalizer.php` used to leave the whole suite green, so the runtime side of per-group `SerializedPath` was unprotected. Three tests now drive it through `ObjectNormalizer`, and reverting that file fails two of them.

Baseline check at the time: 32 of 33 runtime observations byte-identical against 8.2, covering both attributes with and without groups, groups and `'*'` in the context, inheritance, the raw name converter in both directions, both file loaders with the previous syntax, and the existing exception paths.

The three design decisions settled on 2026-08-14 are in the previous comment.
